  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Defense obligated $332B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The department issued 2,687,435 awards with an average award size of $123K, and obligations fell 32.5% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a multi-year rise through FY25 followed by the FY26 to-date level: FY21 $387B, FY22 $414B, FY23 $457B, FY24 $446B, FY25 $492B, FY26 $332B. Aircraft Manufacturing leads NAICS categories with $42.5B in obligations, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $29.2B and Engineering Services at $28.4B. Ship Building and Repairing, Other Aircraft Parts, and several health and systems manufacturing categories also appear among the top ten. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice in the vendor list with $12.7B and $12.6B in obligations; ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION has $11.3B; THE BOEING COMPANY appears with $9B and $6.1B entries. All figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Defense contract spending trended over recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligations rose from FY21 through FY25 and then show the FY26 to-date level. Fiscal-year values are FY21 $387B, FY22 $414B, FY23 $457B, FY24 $446B, FY25 $492B, FY26 $332B. Obligations fell 32.5% year over year into FY26 to date. The FY25 total, $492B, is the largest single-year figure listed."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which sectors and vendors account for most FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest sector at $42.5B, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $29.2B and Engineering Services at $28.4B. Other top NAICS categories include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $24B, and Ship Building and Repairing at $20.3B. Top vendors include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION ($12.7B and $12.6B), ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION ($11.3B), and THE BOEING COMPANY ($9B and $6.1B)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Defense spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense obligated $332B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The department issued 2,687,435 awards with an average award size of $123K, and obligations fell 32.5% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Defense buy?",
      "a": "Defense buys aircraft and related systems, guided missiles and space vehicles, and engineering and research services. Top NAICS categories in FY2026 to date are Aircraft Manufacturing $42.5B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing $29.2B, Engineering Services $28.4B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences $24B, and Ship Building and Repairing $20.3B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Defense's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Defense's largest contractors by obligations in FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION, and THE BOEING COMPANY. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears with $12.7B and $12.6B entries, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION has $11.3B, THE BOEING COMPANY appears with $9B and $6.1B, and other large vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY $8.6B and RTX CORPORATION $3.8B."
